From 7ef7f366f249f1c2712fdfe60943633ad840c136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:56:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): remove avatars from the frontend

Drop every avatar surface from the SPA (server routes, storage and DB
columns stay untouched):

- delete the shared ProfileAvatar component and the chat-agent-avatar
  helper; add chat-agent-label which keeps only the runtime -> display
  name mapping that the chat author rows still use
- account avatar: drop the "user avatar" settings section (upload /
  random / reset), the auth api helpers and the CurrentUser avatar fields
- profile avatar: drop the profile-manager avatar modal, ProfileCard
  avatar, the profiles api helpers + store actions, and the avatar
  fields on the profile types
- chat avatars: drop the assistant avatar (profile + runtime logo) and
  the user avatar from MessageItem, the empty-state logos, the session
  list agent logo + 16px profile avatar, and the now-dead agent props on
  LiveReasoningStatus / SubagentStreamPanel; author rows keep the agent
  and profile names
- kanban: drop the task-card assignee avatar and the avatar lookup in
  KanbanView
- i18n: remove the profiles.avatar and settings.userAvatar namespaces and
  retarget the session-identity toggle copy from avatars to names in all
  11 locales
- keep the coding-agents logo assets (agent manager cards, notification
  icons) and the naive-ui avatarGroupRtl style import
